    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-1900",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0de0627b-2568-5c02-8928-d14344df5a2f",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions",
      "problem": "What is the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x-5cos⁡x$ at the point $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The slope at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is given by the value of the derivative ${y}^{′}$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the derivative, using the fact that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(cos⁡x)=-sin⁡x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-5cos⁡x) \\\\  & =2-5(-sin⁡x) \\\\  & =2+5sin⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(30) & =2+5sin⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2+5(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the instantaneous rate of change is $\\frac{9}{2}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{11}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{9}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{9}{4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{21}{6}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{21}{5}"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "\\frac{9}{2}"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-1900",
        "kp_title": "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions",
        "kp_href": null
      }
