    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-1847",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0de0627b-2568-5c02-8928-d14344df5a2f",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions",
      "problem": "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4cos⁡x+2sin⁡x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin⁡x)=cos⁡x,$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(cos⁡x)=-sin⁡x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4cos⁡x+2sin⁡x) & =4(-sin⁡x)+2(cos⁡x) \\\\  & =2cos⁡x-4sin⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
